> Actual quadratic work, owned history and complete limits

For m=n+1 controls, row lengths are m,m−1,…,1. The number of point blends
and complete stored triangle points are therefore

\[
J=\frac{m(m-1)}2=\frac{n(n+1)}2,\qquad
H=\frac{m(m+1)}2,\qquad\text{coordinate blends}=2J.
\]
\alttext(There are m times m minus one divided by two point blends, m times m plus one divided by two stored triangle points, and twice as many coordinate blends.)

The trace counter increments in the actual inner loop. A point blend updates
two coordinates; its count is not a count of machine instructions or elapsed
time. The scalar evaluator uses O(m) working memory, full tracing O(m²)
history, and subdivision O(m) working/output memory. Sampling k parameters
uses O(m+k) storage and O(m+k(m²+1)) work, including validation once. It is
uniform parameter sampling, without an adaptive chord-error tolerance.

The shape helper cancels factors before checked multiplication. Trace caps
include every initial control and every update, subdivision caps include
both m-point outputs including both copies of their meeting point, and
sampling caps include all k output points and prospective kJ blends. These
checks follow full finite-input validation and precede allocation. Zero
disables only an optional cap; arithmetic and capacity checks remain.
Failures return no partial triangle, child net or misleading truncated curve.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/casteljau_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> degree,actual,theory,stored;
  std::print("| degree n | controls m | actual point blends | predicted n(n+1)/2 | stored points | coordinate blends |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{0,1,2,3,4,8,16,32,64}) {
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_trace(std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanarPoint>(n+1,{1,2}),.5);
    if(a.point_blends!=n*(n+1)/2)return 1;
    degree.push_back(n);actual.push_back(a.point_blends);theory.push_back(n*(n+1)/2);stored.push_back(a.shape.stored_points);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,n+1,a.point_blends,n*(n+1)/2,a.shape.stored_points,a.shape.coordinate_blends);
  }
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::PlanarPoint> c{{0,0},{1,2},{3,3},{4,0}};int rejected=0;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_trace(c,.5,9);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_subdivide(c,.5,7);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_sample(c,4,0,1,4,30);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_sample(c,4,0,1,5,29);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::de_casteljau({},std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN());}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  const double big=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::de_casteljau({{big,0},{big,0}},2);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){++rejected;}
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_trace(c,.5,10);const auto nets=dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_subdivide(c,.5,8);const auto grid=dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_sample(c,4,0,1,5,30);const auto unlimited=dm::algorithms::de_casteljau_trace(c,.5,0);
  if(rejected!=6 || exact.shape.stored_points!=10 || nets.left.size()+nets.right.size()!=8 || grid.size()!=5 || unlimited.point.y!=1.875)return 1;
  std::print("\nComplete triangle/net/sample/work caps, nonfinite parameter and finite-intermediate overflow: {} expected rejections. Exact limits 10,8,5,30 succeed; zero-disabled triangle cap succeeds.\n",rejected);
  std::print("Legacy empty-control sentinel {}; constant singleton {}. These are distinct from subdivision, which requires at least one control.\n",dm::algorithms::de_casteljau({},2),dm::algorithms::de_casteljau({{2,3}},-1));
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.line(degree,actual,"actual blends",{37,99,235},2).points(degree,theory,"n(n+1)/2",{31,41,55},4)
   .line(degree,stored,"stored points",{220,38,38},2).legend({"actual blends","n(n+1)/2","stored points"},{{37,99,235},{31,41,55},{220,38,38}})
   .title("Actual triangular work and complete history grow quadratically")
   .x_label("Bezier degree n").y_label("point blends or retained triangle points")
   .x_limits(0,68).y_limits(0,2700).size(1100,580).save_svg("build/casteljau_work.svg");
}
